TASK: Implement DuckDBFileCompareNodeOperator, Phase 3. Phases 1 and 2 are merged; build on them.

SPEC: docs/specs/duckdb-file-compare.md. Relevant sections: 3 (field table, Config validation), 5.10, 5.11, 5.12, 5.13, 7.
Where the spec differs from existing code conventions, follow the existing code and note it in the PR.

IN SCOPE (Phase 3)
1. Keyless mode (sec 5.10): mode = "keyless". Project both sides onto the same ordered column list
   (compare columns sorted by name), casting a column to VARCHAR on both sides when types differ.
   left_only = L EXCEPT ALL R, right_only = R EXCEPT ALL L. No rules, no keys, no key check
   (warn in summary if they are set). Buckets: MATCH, LEFT_ONLY, RIGHT_ONLY only.
   All objects stay in the job's work schema cmp_<runId>, as in Phase 1.
2. keylessMaxRows guard (sec 5.10): operator-level property, default 1,000,000 rows per side.
   Parquet: row count from file metadata before reading data. CSV: checked right after materialising.
   Over the limit: FAILED with a message telling the user to use keyed mode.
3. Profiling (sec 5.11, 5.13): profiling.enabled + metrics (rowCount, nullCount, distinctCount, min, max)
   from SUMMARIZE on a 1% sample (SUMMARIZE (FROM L USING SAMPLE 1%)); rowCount from the exact table
   count. Mark distinctCount and sampled metrics as approximate in summary.json. Off by default.
4. HTML report (sec 7): output.report.enabled + path. One static, self-contained HTML file (inline CSS,
   no external resources, no JavaScript needed) built by Java from summary data: run info, verdict,
   bucket counts, schema and key findings, threshold results, mismatch count per column (top 50),
   diff sample. HTML-escape every data value.
5. includeMatched (sec 7): write matched.parquet with key columns of MATCH rows when true;
   honours parallelWrite like the other outputs.

OUT OF SCOPE
- Any change to the keyed two-pass compare, validation stages or output contract from Phases 1-2.
- DuckDB connection setup and settings (owned by the existing setup).

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
A. Golden tests for keyless: identical files; duplicate rows counted correctly (multiset semantics);
   a changed row appears once in left_only and once in right_only; type-differing column compared as text;
   keys/rules set in keyless mode produce a warning, not an error.
B. keylessMaxRows: Parquet over limit fails before data is read; CSV over limit fails after
   materialise; at or under limit runs.
C. Profiling: metrics present only when enabled; approximate fields flagged.
D. Report: generated file opens standalone; a value containing <script> is shown escaped.
E. includeMatched true and false both covered.
F. Phase 1 and 2 tests pass unchanged.
